        "original_id": "55de576b-0f82-534a-beab-554bef0d3919",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Manhattan Community Board 6, New York State Assembly\n- People: Brian P. Kavanagh\n- Places: Gramercy Park, Stuyvesant Town, Peter Cooper Village, Waterside Plaza, Murray Hill, Kips Bay, Turtle Bay, Tudor City, Sutton Place, Lower East Side, Union Square, Stuyvesant Square, East Midtown Plaza, Manhattan East Side, East River, East 34th Street, East 40th Street, Madison Avenue\n- Topics: neighborhood boundaries, residential skyscraper complexes, legislative districts\n\nFacts:\n- In 1927, construction of Tudor City commenced, making Tudor City the first residential skyscraper complex in the world.\n- In 1999, Manhattan Community Board 6 defined Murray Hill as bounded by East 34th Street to the south, East 40th Street to the north, Madison Avenue to the west, and the East River to the east.\n- Manhattan Community Board 6 includes the neighborhoods of Gramercy Park, Stuyvesant Town, Peter Cooper Village, Waterside Plaza, Murray Hill, Kips Bay, Turtle Bay, Tudor City, and Sutton Place.\n- Brian P. Kavanagh, born January 18, 1967, is a member of the New York State Assembly representing the 74th Assembly District on the East Side of Manhattan.\n- Brian P. Kavanagh's 74th Assembly District includes parts of the Lower East Side, Union Square, Gramercy Park, Stuyvesant Square, Stuyvesant Town, Peter Cooper Village, East Midtown Plaza, Waterside Plaza, Kips Bay, Murray Hill, Tudor City, and Turtle Bay.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
